From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO pop-up guard settings

A settings page for the pop-up guard, with its own icon from the logo:
a pop-up in front of the page, with the face of the mascot.

- At the top, how many pop-ups and redirects the guard held this week,
  and last week.
- "Hold all pop-ups and redirects": on, CromIKO's default, every
  pop-up and every redirect to another site waits for the user; off,
  only the ones Chromium blocks itself (pop-ups without a tap and its
  redirect interventions). It is the "Block all pop-ups" setting of
  Site settings.
- "Always allowed": the sites allowed with "Always allow" of the
  pop-up guard menu, each with a button that removes it again, so its
  pop-ups and redirects are held again.

The weekly shield report counts the held pop-ups and redirects too:
"Pop-ups held this week" with last week's number, which opens the
page. The count is kept with the other counts of the week, once per
held pop-up or redirect (a page that tries the same one again counts
once), and not for incognito tabs.

